C03: installing known software absent from the Start catalog is answered by its absence (INSTALL1629)

Four open rows ask BAXY to install Photoshop. The product installs no Adobe software by name: there is no winget package and the installation needs the vendor's installer and account. Such a request now reads app.installed with the name as the person wrote it — the known-software list already lets an opening of absent software be answered by the same read — and the composer says the application is not in the Windows Start catalog and that installing it is done with the vendor's own installer, as a fact, without denying a capability or offering a download. Registry-wide diff: the four Photoshop literals; nothing else changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


